  26:     Move the source-color pixels into the unique outline interior whose size matches the source count.
  27: 
  28:     Input structure
  29:     - The grid has a dominant background and exactly two foreground colors.
  30:     - One foreground color forms 8-connected outline objects with row-wise interior cells.
  31:     - The other foreground color supplies a set of source pixels away from the chosen outline.
  32:     Rule
  33:     - For each possible outline color, compute each 8-connected outline object's
  34:       row-span interior: background pixels strictly between the leftmost and
  35:       rightmost outline pixels on each occupied row.
  36:     - Select the unique outline interior whose cell count equals the total
  37:       number of pixels of the other foreground color.
  38:     - Erase the source pixels and paint that matched interior with the source color.
  39:     Key insight
  40:     - The colors are roles, not fixed IDs: the source color is identified by
  41:       counting, and the destination is the outline with a matching interior area.
  42:     """
